---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config.mjs';
import { ui } from '../i18n/en.mjs';
---

<Layout title={`Privacy Policy – ${ui.siteName}`} description={`Read the privacy policy for ${ui.siteName}: a static Bible verse tool with no accounts that never sends your verse, topic, or search terms to any server.`}>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: October 18, 2026</em></p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} (“this site”) is a static website. It has no user accounts, and the core tool runs
    entirely in your browser. We do not ask for your name, email address, or any other personal
    information in order to use it.
  </p>

  <h2>What the tool does and does not send</h2>
  <p>
    When you generate a verse, the random selection happens locally on your device using a small
    verse library bundled with the site. Your chosen topic and the verse you receive are
    <strong>never</strong> transmitted to us or to any analytics service.
  </p>
  <p>
    The search and browse tools also run entirely in your browser. Your search terms are
    <strong>never</strong> sent to us or to any third party; results are matched locally against the
    verse text bundled with the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Find a Verse (on-device semantic search)</h2>
  <p>
    The “Find a Verse” tool matches what you type to a verse using a small language model and a
    precomputed search index that run <strong>entirely on your device</strong>. The model and index
    are downloaded once as ordinary website files (like images or scripts) and are then cached by
    your browser for reuse. Your query text is processed only in your browser and is
    <strong>never</strong> sent to us, to any AI service, or to any third party. It is also never
    placed in the page address, stored in analytics, or written to logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your browser or device cannot run the model, the tool falls back to simple local keyword
    matching, still with no data leaving your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If analytics is enabled for this site, it uses Google Analytics 4 to understand aggregate usage
    (for example, which pages are visited and what kind of device is used). Any analytics we enable
    is configured to record only generic, non-identifying events. It is never configured to collect
    verse text, verse references, chosen topics, or other user-generated input. Google Analytics may
    use cookies or similar technologies; you can opt out of Google Analytics across the web using
    Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not set its own cookies. If analytics is enabled, Google Analytics may set cookies
    as described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Saved verses (local storage)</h2>
  <p>
    If you save a verse, it is stored only in your browser’s local storage on your own device, along
    with any private note you add to it. It is never sent to us or to any third party, and it is removed
    if you clear this site’s data in your browser. You can export your saved verses to a file or import
    them back into your browser — the file stays on your device and is never uploaded.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same applies to your reading settings (text size and spacing), your reading-plan progress, and
    your reading check-in streak — these are kept only in your browser’s local storage and are never
    sent to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we will use your email address only to respond to your message and will not add
    you to any mailing list or share it with anyone else.
    {CONTACT_EMAIL ? <> You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</> : ''}
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights such as access, correction, or deletion of
    personal data. Because this site does not directly collect personal data from you, there is
    generally nothing for us to access, correct, or delete. If you have questions about this policy,
    please use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when it was
    last revised.
  </p>
</Layout>
